Subject: [PATCH 0177] santoni: declare the private processor-binding API

The opt-in CPU probe uses thread_bind, whose declaration is hidden
from exported IOKit headers. Use its existing C ABI explicitly,
rather than enabling broad private headers. No runtime/input change.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp
@@ -28,6 +28,8 @@
 extern "C" void flush_dcache64(addr64_t addr, unsigned count, int phys);
 extern "C" vm_offset_t ml_io_map(vm_offset_t phys_addr, vm_size_t size);
 extern "C" int printf(const char *format, ...);
+/* sched_prim.h omits this private API from the IOKit exported headers. */
+extern "C" processor_t thread_bind(processor_t processor);
 
 #if defined(SANTONI)
 /* Matches the assembly's private cache-line slot; no neighboring CPU writes. */
